# issues/fixed/numeric-conversion-of-a-non-numeric-source-checks-clean-and-emits-a-hollow-stub.md:
# `usize(s)` with a String source (likewise a bool or a raw pointer) took the
# evaluator's "non-numeric soft fallback" — an UnknownVal of the target type
# and no lowering — so `check` passed and codegen emitted an abort() stub. The
# fallback is now reserved for UNRESOLVED sources (the unit placeholder, an
# open type variable); a concrete non-numeric source is a check error. The kept
# substring is the diagnostic; the rest of the rendering carries the sandbox
# path.
stdout_keep_match=Cannot convert a value of type [^:]+ to usize
timeout=120
